KG42.register("clusters-e0d0bc3affb51b1f5b9fc905",{"id":"32-wholesale_prosumer_storage::v142-d-K003","paper":"32-wholesale_prosumer_storage","label":"Local P2P price interval and conditional network fee reduction proposal","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K003","label":"Local P2P price interval and conditional network fee reduction proposal","market_meaning":"For local P2P trading, a price that changes every half hour is adopted, and the price interval is defined by the feed-in compensation price and the grid electricity purchase price; under the condition that local trading does not use the transmission network, the proposed price with a 27.6% fee reduction is retained. The external payment price is used only to explain the comparison benchmark, and the compatibility of the actual proposed price with the interval remains to be confirmed.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM","LEM_DEM"],"process_stages":["pricing","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"R005 is limited to local P2P pricing, and R010 shares only the comparison background of external feed-in and electricity purchase prices and does not constitute a local payment rule. The meanings of the feed-in prices are compatible, but the different names for the grid electricity purchase price have not yet been clarified, and the reduction proposal does not automatically guarantee satisfaction of the price interval.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The choice of local price has independent market significance and cannot be merged into the joint allocation rule because it shares external prices with the community cost objective. A shared price reference does not establish a logical dependence of the local price on the external payment formula, nor does it presume complete internal settlement.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the price update frequency, the comparison interval, and the conditional network fee reduction proposal."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R010","ownership":"shared","role":"context","rationale":"Used only to explain the comparative meaning of the external feed-in compensation price and the day-ahead grid electricity purchase price; external transaction payments are not converted into P2P charging obligations."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-p002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-pF"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e07","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g02-e36","v141-b-g02-e37"],"rationale":"The same feed-in compensation price is used respectively for external compensation accounting and for comparison with the local price lower bound; the common quantity identity does not create an additional payment dependency."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-pDAG"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-p001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e07","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g02-e37"],"rationale":"The two records may be different names for the same day-ahead grid electricity purchase price, assuming the roles of local price comparison and external pricing respectively; the source does not clarify the alias, so only a candidate association is retained."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-M01","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-pF","v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-p002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e07","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g02-e36"],"rationale":"Both parameters are the hourly feed-in compensation price under the same mechanism; the local roles of price lower-bound comparison and payment accounting are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-M02","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-pDAG","v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-p001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e07","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g02-e37"],"rationale":"p_DA_G and p_G_DA have close semantics, but the available materials do not clarify a unified notation and price convention for them; no representative is selected, nor is the same quantity confirmed."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G01","category":"unverified_source","description":"The price interval, the 27.6% reduction proposal, and the meaning of external prices all come from B evidence that has not yet been independently audited; this cluster is not a scientifically confirmed pricing system.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e02","v141-b-g02-e07","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g02-e36","v141-b-g02-e37"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequently check the original text, price convention, and the applicability conditions of the proposal; this round maintains the unaudited candidate status."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G02","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"There is not yet a clear symbol correspondence among p_DA_G in R005, p_DA in Table 1, and p_G_DA in Eq. (15); price parameters cannot be unified merely because their subscripts are similar.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-pDAG","v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-p001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e07","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g02-e34","v141-b-g02-e37"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the original text and the price data definitions to confirm whether they are the same electricity purchase price including fees, and then have the upstream decide the alias relation; until then, keep the records separate."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G03","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The reduction proposal in R005-C003 does not automatically guarantee satisfaction of the upper and lower bounds in C002. The current chain lacks hourly price conditions and compatibility verification, and it is not clarified whether the proposal is the value actually adopted.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-pF","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-pDAG"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e07","v141-b-g02-e34","v141-b-g02-e36","v141-b-g02-e37"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Confirm the implementation status and price convention of the proposed price and check hourly interval compatibility; if incompatible, retain it as an unresolved conditional problem, and do not independently add truncation or a substitute pricing formula."}]},"rule_refs":["32-wholesale_prosumer_storage::v141-c-R005","32-wholesale_prosumer_storage::v141-c-R010"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-739917e3869e45a6","COMP-8194bc76303bef38","COMP-f8b6dd7cb8a348ad"]});
